===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=bag|:inh|enm:male<id:bag>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|male|id=bag}}, from {{der|en|xno|male}}, {{der|en|fro|male||bag, wallet}}, from {{der|en|frk|*malhu|*malha|t=bag}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*malhō||bag, pouch}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*molko-||leather pouch}}. Compare {{cog|nl|maal}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|now|_|regional}} A [[bag]] or [[wallet]]. {{defdate|from 13<sup>th</sup>c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1499|author=w:John Skelton|title=The Bowge of Courte
|passage=What, loo, man, see here of dyce a bale; / A brydelynge caste for that is in thy '''male'''!}}
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|page=25|passage=Open the '''Males''', yet guard the treaſure ſure.<br>Lay out our golden wedges to the view,<br>That their reflexions may amaze the Perſeans.}}
# A [[bag]] containing [[letter]]s to be delivered by post.
# {{senseid|en|physical material conveyed by the postal service}} The (physical) material conveyed by the postal service. {{defdate|from 17<sup>th</sup>c.}}
#: {{syn|en|snail mail}}
#: {{ant|en|email<id:quantity of messages, mass sense>|mail<id:email messages, mass sense>}}
#: {{mer|en|mailpiece}}
#: {{ux|en|Don't forget to pick up the '''mail''' on your way.}}
#* '''1823''', ''[http://books.google.com/books?id=FsQHAAAAQAAJ The stranger in Liverpool; or, An historical and descriptive view of the town of Liverpool and its environs]'', Seventh Edition, T. Kaye, [http://books.google.com/books?id=FsQHAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA96 page 96],
#*: The following are the hours at which the letter-box of this office is closed for making up the several '''mails''', and the hours at which each '''mail''' is despatched: &para; {{...}}
#* '''1887''', John Houston Merrill (editor), ''[http://books.google.com/books?id=75ENAAAAYAAJ The American and English Encyclop&aelig;dia of Law]'', Volume I, Edward Thompson, [http://books.google.com/books?id=75ENAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA121 p.121],
#*: If he retains the account, and permits several '''mails''' to pass without objecting to it, he will be held to have admitted its correctness.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1944|month=July and August|author=Charles E. Lee|title=The "City of Truro"|journal=Railway Magazine|page=202|text=The transfer by tender of some 1,300 mail bags was effected smartly, and the "Ocean '''Mails''' Special" train was ready at 9.19 a.m.}}
## {{lb|en|chiefly|_|US|uncountable}} The [[letter]]s, [[parcel]]s, etc. delivered to a particular address or person. {{defdate|from 19<sup>th</sup>c.}}
##: {{ux|en|It should be in your '''mail''' today, unless the post office lost it!}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} A stagecoach, train or ship that delivers such post.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1950|month=April|author=Timothy H. Cobb|title=The Kenya-Uganda Railway|journal=Railway Magazine|page=263|text=All trains stop at all stations, with the exception of a few "local" stations near Mombasa and an odd flag stop or two usually missed by the '''mails'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1962|month=December|title=Motive Power Miscellany: North Eastern Region|journal=Modern Railways|pages=422, 425|text=On the morning after the one-day strike, October 4, one of the Type 4s on crew-training, No. D169, was appropriated to head the 3 a.m. '''mail''' to Hull, as no steam locomotive had been lit up and the usual Hull Type 3 was not available; [...].}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 January 12|author=Benedict le Vay|title=The heroes of Soham...|journal=RAIL|issue=948|page=42|text=As he passed though the station, he slowed to yell to the signalman, Frank 'Sailor' Bridges: "Sailor - have you anything between here and Fordham? Where's the '''mail'''?" Gimbert knew the mail train was due, and he didn't want to endanger another train with his burning bomb wagon.}}
# {{senseid|en|postal service or system}} The postal service or system in general. {{defdate|from 17<sup>th</sup>c.}}
#: {{syn|en|post<l:UK,Ireland,India,Australia,New Zealand>}}
#: {{ux|en|He decided to send his declaration by '''mail'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|email service}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[electronic mail|Electronic mail]], [[e-mail]]: a [[computer]] [[network]]–based service for sending, storing, and forwarding electronic messages. {{defdate|from 20<sup>th</sup>c.}}
#: {{syn|en|email<id:message system or service>}}
#: {{ux|en|Yahoo '''Mail''' has been providing mail service since 1997.}}
# {{senseid|en|email messages, mass sense}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[email|Email]] [[message]]s conceived in bulk (as with the analogous sense of [[#English:_physical material conveyed by the postal service|physical mail]]).
#: {{syn|en|email<id:quantity of messages, mass sense>}}
#: {{collocation|en|You've got '''mail''' [old audio clip announcing new email in the 1990s-2000s]}}
# {{senseid|en|one email message}} {{lb|en|countable|especially|Indian English}} An [[email]] [[message]].
#: {{syn|en|email<id:one message, count sense>}}
#: {{ux|en|Please look through those '''mails''' and confirm whether you received the one about scheduling.}}
# A trunk, box, or bag, in which clothing, etc., may be carried.
#* {{RQ:Scott Bride of Lammermoor|passage=“Fetch me the little private '''mail''' with the padlocks, that I recommended to your particular charge — d'ye hear?”}}

